{#-
  One part of the story for Procreator to rewrite to fit the owner's change (procreator/rewrite.ts):
  a scene's passages, or the reference, memory and the owner's sheets. The book and the cast first,
  then what changed, then the numbered passages, and the task last. Takes a RewriteView.
-#}
<book>
Title: {{ book.title }}
Length: {{ book.length }}
Style: {{ book.style }}
Point of view: {{ book.pov }}
How dark it goes: {{ book.darkness }}
</book>

<cast>
{{ cast | join(', ') }}
</cast>

<owner_change>
{% for c in changed %}
<changed subject="{{ c.subject }}">
{% for f in c.fields %}
<field name="{{ f.name }}">
<was>{{ f.was if f.was else 'Nothing.' }}</was>
<now>{{ f.now if f.now else 'Nothing.' }}</now>
</field>
{% endfor %}
</changed>
{% endfor %}
</owner_change>

<passages part="{{ part }}">
{% for p in passages %}
<passage n="{{ loop.index }}" where="{{ p.where }}">
{{ p.text }}
</passage>
{% endfor %}
</passages>

<task>
{% for r in renames %}
- {{ r.was }} is called {{ r.now }} now, and always was. Change every form of the name {{ r.was }} that means them (with a possessive, a nickname or a short form made from it) to the matching form of {{ r.now }}. Leave alone words that only look like it.
{% endfor %}
{% for name in writtenOut %}
- {{ name }} was never in the story. Write them out of these passages: what they did and said goes, or falls to no one, and each passage still reads whole.
{% endfor %}
{% if pov %}
- The book's point of view is now "{{ pov.now }}", where it was "{{ pov.was }}". Rewrite each narration and each chapter of the book whole in the new one, keeping everything that happens and every word that's said. Nothing but the narration and the book changes its point of view.
{% endif %}
{% if always %}
- The rest of the change above holds always: rewrite whatever in these passages says otherwise.
{% endif %}
Rewrite the passages above to fit, with rewrite_passages.
</task>
